            "text": "{\"primary_meaning\":\"Divine presence, holiness, truth, and revelation, most fully realized in Jesus Christ as the source of salvation and spiritual life, standing in stark contrast to the darkness of sin, evil, and ignorance.\",\"primary_basis\":[\"1 John 1:5\",\"John 8:12\",\"John 1:4-5\",\"Isaiah 9:2\",\"Psalm 27:1\"],\"alternatives\":[{\"meaning\":\"The moral witness and righteous conduct of believers reflecting God's nature in a fallen world.\",\"basis\":[\"Matthew 5:14-16\",\"Philippians 2:15\"],\"prominence\":\"common\"},{\"meaning\":\"The Word of God, divine law, and practical spiritual guidance for living.\",\"basis\":[\"Psalm 119:105\",\"Proverbs 6:23\"],\"prominence\":\"common\"},{\"meaning\":\"The mechanism of divine judgment and the exposure of hidden sin or falsehood.\",\"basis\":[\"Ephesians 5:13\",\"John 3:19-21\"],\"prominence\":\"minority\"},{\"meaning\":\"General gladness, joy, deliverance, and prosperity for God's people.\",\"basis\":[\"Esther 8:16\",\"Psalm 97:11\"],\"prominence\":\"minority\"}],\"has_settled_consensus\":true,\"confidence\":\"high\",\"notes\":\"The symbolism of light is one of the most pervasive and universally recognized motifs in biblical literature, operating heavily within a dualistic framework where light inherently opposes darkness.\"}",
